- **childrenOf**: There is no explicit `childrenOf` reference in this method. Child navigation is handled internally by the `AST_NODE_ADAPTER` node adapter passed to the `TreeTransformer`, not by any direct call within `transform`.

## What It Returns

The method returns a `Node` — the result of the tree transformation, described in the code comment as the "changed root."

**Regarding Document vs. operation/fragment root:** The method returns whatever `root` was configured through the builder, transformed. Since the builder allows specifying an arbitrary `root` (the docs note fragment spreads must be "processed explicitly by supplying them as root"), the returned node corresponds to that supplied root — it is not inherently a full Document. It reflects the root node the caller provided, which could be an operation or fragment root.

